# =============================================================================
# muons_dt_mucf_stopping.mac
#
# Stage 2 of the muon-catalyzed fusion (muCF) chain: stop negative muons
# in a liquid D-T cell. The stopping distribution from this run defines
# where the muCF cycle would take place (each stopped mu- catalyzes
# ~10^2 D-T fusions within its 2.2 us lifetime, with ~1% alpha-sticking
# loss per cycle).
#
# NOTE Geant4 does NOT model the muCF cycle itself (muonic-atom
# formation, d-mu -> t-mu transfer, resonant dt-mu molecule formation,
# in-molecule fusion, sticking). In this simulation a stopped mu-
# undergoes the standard muMinusCaptureAtRest / decay competition. Use
# the stopping distribution from this run as input to a parametric
# cycle model and source the fusion products with neutrons_dt_14MeV.mac
# and alphas_dt_3p5MeV.mac. See macros/README.md.
#
# Detector: gdml/dt_target_mucf.gdml
#   - World:  60×60×100 cm vacuum
#   - Vessel: stainless steel, 2 mm walls (~1.6 g/cm2 entrance window)
#   - Target: 10×10×20 cm liquid D-T (0.18 g/cm3), entrance face at z = 0
#
# Beam:
#   - Particle : mu-
#   - Energy   : Gaussian, mean 22 MeV, sigma 1.5 MeV. After the steel
#                window this stops at ~7 cm depth in the D-T, with the
#                energy spread distributing stops over several cm.
#   - Position : upstream on the beam axis (z = -20 cm)
#   - Direction: along +z
#
# Stopping-distribution extraction (in ROOT, z in mm; last step of the
# primary muon track):
#   tree->Draw("step_postZ>>h(240,-20,220)", "step_trackID==1 && step_kinE<0.01")
# =============================================================================

# --- Load geometry ---
/detector/readGDML gdml/dt_target_mucf.gdml

# --- Physics ---
/run/initialize

# --- Beam ---
/gun/particle    mu-
/gun/energyMode  gauss
/gun/energy      22 MeV
/gun/gaussSigma  1.5 MeV
/gun/position    0 0 -20 cm
/gun/direction   0 0 1

# --- Run ---
/run/printProgress 200
/run/beamOn 2000
